# New Page Documentation Gate

Before a new page (route entry in `routeConfig.js`) ships, two docs **must** exist
under `apps/delivery-ops/docs/pages/`:

| Doc | Filename pattern | Required sections |
|---|---|---|
| Requirements | `{PageName}-requirements.md` | Purpose, Audiences, User Stories, UI Behaviour, Permissions, Edge Cases, Acceptance Criteria |
| Data & Middleware | `{PageName}-data-layer.md` | API endpoints called, server route → service → JIRA mapping, data shapes, caching strategy, error handling |

## Hard rule

Do **not** add a route to `routeConfig.js` or wire up a new `<Page />` in `App.js`
without first creating both docs. If asked to add a page without them, create the
docs as part of the same task before touching the route config.

## Retrofit obligation

When you **edit** any existing page file (component, hook, route handler, or service)
for a page that is missing its docs, you must create the missing docs in that same
session. Do not leave the gap wider than you found it.

## Doc location

```
apps/delivery-ops/docs/pages/
  EmailSender-requirements.md
  EmailSender-data-layer.md
  ProjectStatus-requirements.md
  ProjectStatus-data-layer.md
  ...
```

## Never do

- Add a route to `routeConfig.js` without both docs present
- Ship a new page component without a requirements doc
- Treat a skill file or AGENTS.md as a substitute for a page requirements doc
